cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Affinity Intelligence: A Physicochemical-Feature-Based Protein-Protein Binding Affinity Ranking Engine"
abstract: >-
  Affinity Intelligence is a CPU-only protein-protein binding affinity (ΔG)
  ranking engine. It extracts physicochemical interface features from a complex
  3D structure (buried surface area ΔSASA, hydrogen bonds, salt bridges, contact
  density, interface residue composition), deliberately strips out pure
  size/volume confounders in favour of normalized intensity features, and trains
  a LightGBM regressor on the public PPB-Affinity dataset. Train/test splitting
  is performed at the 40% sequence-identity family level so that no protein
  family crosses the split, eliminating homology leakage. On a family-isolated
  test set (950 rows / 437 unseen families) the model reaches a Spearman rank
  correlation of 0.534 with an RMSE of 2.37 kcal/mol. Because the model is
  intentionally oriented toward wet-lab prioritization, we recommend using its
  relative ranking output ("stronger than X% of training interfaces") rather
  than the absolute predicted ΔG, whose magnitude is shrunk (fitted slope 0.24).
